   "t": "chapter",
   "n": "IV",
   "text": "The Faith Received",
   "id": "tfr"
  },
  {
   "t": "eyebrow",
   "text": "What it is"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "text": "The Christian tradition is the Christian’s inheritance"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "The Faith Received gathers the church’s own writings into one free library: Migne’s Latin and Greek fathers, the councils and creeds, the medieval doctors, the Reformation confessions and the English books printed before 1700."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "For centuries these texts sat in research libraries, untranslated and unsearchable. Now a pastor can read the fathers on a phone, see where the church’s teachers cite Romans 8 and trace a doctrine from Nicaea to Westminster."
  },
